      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Not sure if i'm wrong but problems i'm expecting from this implementation is that: By default all users when noticing this option will decide to set it either \"very low to download faster\" or \"higher for more stable performance\".\n\nWebsites often have different limits from one another, the point of this limitation is to address getting rate limited by various services on accident.\n\nHowever.. If users set it too low and then images fail to load making an experience worse because of the rate-limit.. They will blame the world or VRChat for this behavior because that's how people usually react.\n\nGiving control over the rate-limit of external services into hands of a user/world sounds like a disaster waiting to happen since majority won't exactly know the impact of such option.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2023-03-10T03:12:49.242Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Dynamic images take too long to render with the current limits, its neutering the individual experience. \n\nIt would be better to allow the user to set a local decision. It makes more sense for individuals to decide which is best for themselves rather than a forced arbitrary default. Make it a setting like \"Max Avatar Download Size\" and just rename that section into \"Download Options.\"\n\n***Why?***\n\n- Uses can keep decide if the update rate is right for them\n\n- Data capped users can raise the seconds per image update\n\n- Security is up to the User, as the rest of VRC\n\n***How?***\n\n- Individual setting in the menu (With the *New* Menu 2.0 that's more flexible ╰(*°▽°*)╯) \n\n- You already have the \" Avatar file size\", hook the update rate into it instead of",
